    "frames": [
      {
        "slide": 1,
        "role": "cover",
        "subject": "A space-filling teaching model of two protein chains seated together on a dark plinth on the lab bench, bone resin on the left and brass on the right, the brass running off the right edge. Under the headline 'An AI was asked which proteins pair up', it gives a reader the question the deck asks as one object: two separate bodies that fit together. The pair covers about 40 percent of the frame at 432 px.",
        "visual_consequence": "Two distinct chains in two materials, matte pale resin and specular brass, press into each other along one seam. They read as a pair at feed size without the headline. The brass is the deck's only warm metal and arrives here as the second partner.",
        "weakness": "The cool grey slab is gone; the stand top under the brass chain is dark warm brown and the footer band falls to black. Residuals: a cool grey sliver about 50 by 60 native px at the far right edge behind the lowest brass spheres (r3c2 x 1030 to 1080, y 380 to 440); soft contact under the bone chain; the light behind the model is a broad warm wash rather than a seam, and the topmost bone spheres fall to cool grey. None breaks the subject at native size.",
        "repair": "None required for the audition. In a polish pass, narrow the stage pool at the far right so the grey sliver goes to the stand's brown.",
