        "subject": "The black milled plate in plan view, with the half-matrix triangle cut into roughly 210 square tiles of one size by V grooves. One brass tile stands proud near the right angle and casts down and to the right across two neighbours.",
        "visual_consequence": "Without the headline, the reader sees that one tile among about two hundred identical ones is the whole find. The tile count matches 630,003 divided by 2,895 at the triangle's own scale. The brass is the only warm thing in the frame, so 0.46 percent reads as one small unit against a field.",
        "weakness": "None blocking. In r3c2 the brass tile is about 45 design px on a side, inside design x 886 to 931 and y 1036 to 1080. Its top now shows a warm diagonal specular sweep, its bevel is lit on the key sides, and it reads as polished brass. The leader dot sits on its lower edge. The grooves have one lit wall and one shadowed wall, the hypotenuse is a clean saw edge with cut half tiles, and the terrace casts onto the plate below and to its right. Minor: the brass tile's cast ends in a soft vertical cut at about design x 987, so the shadow looks clipped to a tile column rather than tapering. The tile tops show almost none of the tool marks the craft row names, so they read as dark satin rather than milled aluminium. Neither weakens the argument at feed size.",
